From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psX workspace <psx@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:40:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: enable PS4 DP-bridge audio AFMT setup

The Liverpool/Gladius DP-to-HDMI bridge path reports a DP encoder, so
dce_v8_0_encoder_mode_set() never calls dce_v8_0_afmt_enable() or
dce_v8_0_afmt_setmode().  The DTO patch restored the audio reference
clock, but the AFMT/ACR/60958/audio-endpoint setup is still skipped.
Native 48 kHz playback is robotic while 44.1 kHz is clean
(EXP-20261021-055).

Assign and enable the AFMT for the PS4 DP encoder and run the existing
audio setup for that path.  Keep the DTO programming in
dce_v8_0_crtc_mode_set().  The PS4 encoder reports INTERNAL_UNIPHY with
enc_mode=DP, so the DP condition must not depend on a named DP-bridge
encoder ID.  The DRM_INFO markers are diagnostic for the test boot.

This is a test patch. It was applied in EXP-20261021-056/057: the AFMT
setup runs on the PS4 DP encoder but native 48 kHz remains robotic. It is
retained as negative evidence and is not applied in the default series.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v8_0.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v8_0.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v8_0.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v8_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v8_0.c
@@ -3318,6 +3318,7 @@ dce_v8_0_encoder_mode_set(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 			  struct drm_display_mode *mode,
 			  struct drm_display_mode *adjusted_mode)
 {
+	struct amdgpu_device *adev = drm_to_adev(encoder->dev);
 	struct amdgpu_encoder *amdgpu_encoder = to_amdgpu_encoder(encoder);
 
 	amdgpu_encoder->pixel_clock = adjusted_mode->clock;
@@ -3328,7 +3329,21 @@ dce_v8_0_encoder_mode_set(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 	/* set scaler clears this on some chips */
 	dce_v8_0_set_interleave(encoder->crtc, mode);
 
-	if (amdgpu_atombios_encoder_get_encoder_mode(encoder) == ATOM_ENCODER_MODE_HDMI) {
+	if (adev->asic_type == CHIP_LIVERPOOL || adev->asic_type == CHIP_GLADIUS)
+		DRM_INFO("PS4 audio: mode_set asic=%d enc_mode=%d bridge=%d\n",
+			 adev->asic_type,
+			 amdgpu_atombios_encoder_get_encoder_mode(encoder),
+			 amdgpu_encoder_get_dp_bridge_encoder_id(encoder));
+
+	if (amdgpu_atombios_encoder_get_encoder_mode(encoder) == ATOM_ENCODER_MODE_HDMI ||
+	    ((adev->asic_type == CHIP_LIVERPOOL || adev->asic_type == CHIP_GLADIUS) &&
+	     amdgpu_atombios_encoder_get_encoder_mode(encoder) == ATOM_ENCODER_MODE_DP)) {
+		struct amdgpu_encoder_atom_dig *dig = amdgpu_encoder->enc_priv;
+
+		DRM_INFO("PS4 audio: setup enc_mode=%d dig=%d afmt=%d enabled=%d\n",
+			 amdgpu_atombios_encoder_get_encoder_mode(encoder),
+			 dig ? dig->dig_encoder : -1, dig && dig->afmt,
+			 dig && dig->afmt && dig->afmt->enabled);
 		dce_v8_0_afmt_enable(encoder, true);
 		dce_v8_0_afmt_setmode(encoder, adjusted_mode);
 	}
@@ -3347,7 +3362,9 @@ static void dce_v8_0_encoder_prepare(struct drm_encoder *encoder)
 		struct amdgpu_encoder_atom_dig *dig = amdgpu_encoder->enc_priv;
 		if (dig) {
 			dig->dig_encoder = dce_v8_0_pick_dig_encoder(encoder);
-			if (amdgpu_encoder->active_device & ATOM_DEVICE_DFP_SUPPORT)
+			if ((amdgpu_encoder->active_device & ATOM_DEVICE_DFP_SUPPORT) ||
+			    ((adev->asic_type == CHIP_LIVERPOOL || adev->asic_type == CHIP_GLADIUS) &&
+			     amdgpu_encoder_get_dp_bridge_encoder_id(encoder) != ENCODER_OBJECT_ID_NONE))
 				dig->afmt = adev->mode_info.afmt[dig->dig_encoder];
 		}
 	}
